          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em pure state
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state on a star-algebra
            which is an extremal point in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex set
            of all states.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            is (in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bayesian+interpretation+of+quantum+mechanics"} Bayesian interpretation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \leq \phi
            means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            contains all of the information of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            (and possibly more). A
            %strong pure state
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal element
            of this poset: a state that specifies as much information as possible about the system. A
            %strong mixed state
            is a state that is not pure.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Fairly generally, a physical system has a complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            (or more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+algebra"} unital
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebra"} star algebra
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state
            is a positive-semidefinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho\colon \mathcal{A} \to \mathbb{C}
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(1) = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            as a convex-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
            of two other states:
          #eq:combo.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mi σ
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho = a \sigma + b \tau ,
          %p
            where necessarily
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq a, b \leq 1
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b = 1
          %p
            The state
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is
            %strong pure
            if, whenever
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:combo"} (1)
            holds for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \neq \tau
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = 0
            (hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = 1
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo =
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho = \tau
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = 1
            (hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = 0
            and
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo =
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho = \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            is
            %strong mixed
            if we ever have
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:combo"} (1)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \neq \tau
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi a
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt a \lt 1
            (hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi b
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt b \lt 1
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \neq \sigma, \tau
          %p
            Really, this definition makes sense as long as the states form a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
          %p
            To define when one state gives at least as much information as another (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
            from the Idea section), let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \leq \sigma
            mean that the
            %span.newWikiWord
              mutual information
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/mutual+information"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(\rho,\sigma)
            equals the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(\rho)
            %span.newWikiWord
              conditional entropy
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/conditional+entropy"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(\rho|\sigma)
            is zero. (In the classical case, this partial order is attributed to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Shannon1953"} Shannon (1953)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LiChong2011"} Li &amp; Chong (2011)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+elements"} maximal elements
            under this partial order should be precisely the pure states, but the direct definition of pure states is much simpler.
          .query
            %p
              I need to check whether these are equivalent on any
              = succeed "-algebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
          %h2#special_cases Special cases
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the algebra of continuous complex-valued functions on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong pure states
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            correspond precisely to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/points"} points
            in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
            (at least for a compact
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+measure"} Radon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measures"} probability measures
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+delta+measure"} Dirac delta measure
          %p
            On the other hand, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the algebra of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operators"} bounded operators
            on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            correspond precisely to the rays in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|\psi\rangle}{\langle\psi|}
            for some unit vector
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|\psi\rangle}
          %h2#classical_versus_quantum Classical versus quantum
          %p
            In any case, a pure state is a state of maximal information, while a mixed state is a state with less than maximal information. In the classical case, we may say that a pure state is a state of
            %em complete
            information, but this does not work in the quantum case; from the perspective of the information-theoretic or Bayesian interpretation of quantum physics, this inability to have complete information, even when having maximal information, is the key feature of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            that distinguishes it from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+physics"} classical physics
